Summary
- pdf_inspect.py uses optional pypdf to report the page count, author and title,
  then writes text extracted from the first page to a deterministic output path.
  Missing files, missing pypdf and malformed PDFs are reported without traceback.
- compare_libs.py compares pypdf, pdfplumber and pymupdf (imported as fitz),
  records elapsed time, extracted-text length, status and errors, and writes JSON.
  A missing or failing backend does not stop the remaining comparisons.
- The default input is a small synthetic local PDF fixture. No report was
  downloaded and no network access is needed by the tools or tests.
- pyproject.toml keeps runtime dependencies empty and exposes all three PDF
  libraries through the optional exploration dependency group.

